{
  "name": "143. Mistral content arrays return text or explicit streaming errors (#7906) (mistral-content-array)",
  "description": "Deterministic, free fixture pin for #7906. A local SSE upstream emits original Mistral delta.content arrays through the real native provider parser. Three routes complete homogeneous text arrays; three routes stream a leading thinking block as reasoning followed by the answer text in the same delta (the zai-glm/magistral shape); text-then-thinking and reference arrays terminate with a structured error instead of being dropped. Uses real dashboard login, a fresh app profile with no preexisting Mistral, an owned native provider with a dummy key, upstream wire witness and cleanup. Mistral is not a supported custom-provider base in this revision, so no allowlist changes or bypass mocker plugin are used. Same-host fixture started by run-mistral-content-array-fixture.mjs; scoped INCLUDE_PREVIEW=1 PARALLEL=0 only. User-run live harness; complete preparation below.\n\nUser-run setup (Linux/WSL Bash, repo root; Node, Go, jq, curl, docker, nc and lsof):\n1. Start the profile backing service: docker compose -f tests/docker-compose.yml up -d weaviate. Wait for curl -sf http://localhost:9000/v1/.well-known/ready and nc -z localhost 50051 to succeed. Check lsof -nP -iTCP:3021 -sTCP:LISTEN prints no listener; use another free port consistently if occupied.\n2. Make a fresh isolated profile (never run this on an existing app directory):\nmkdir -p tmp\nTASK_MISTRAL_APP_DIR=$(mktemp -d \"$PWD/tmp/mistral-content-array.XXXXXX\")\ngit show HEAD:tests/integrations/python/config.json | jq --arg db \"$TASK_MISTRAL_APP_DIR/config.db\" --arg logs \"$TASK_MISTRAL_APP_DIR/logs.db\" '.providers={} | .governance.routing_rules=[] | .governance.virtual_keys=[] | .governance.auth_config={\"is_enabled\":true,\"admin_username\":\"mistral_array_harness\",\"admin_password\":\"harness-only-password\"} | .config_store.config.path=$db | .logs_store.config.path=$logs | .mcp.client_configs=[] | .client.oauth2_server_config.issuer_url=\"http://localhost:3021\"' > \"$TASK_MISTRAL_APP_DIR/config.json\"\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$TASK_MISTRAL_APP_DIR\" > tmp/mistral-content-array-app-dir\n3. In a separate terminal, start only the same-host fixture (ENV_FILE must not already exist; choose another path for concurrent runs):\nnode tests/e2e/api/runners/run-mistral-content-array-fixture.mjs --env-out tmp/mistral-content-array.env.json\n4. Start the gateway from the reviewed source in another terminal:\nmake dev PORT=3021 APP_DIR=$(cat tmp/mistral-content-array-app-dir)\n5. After /health answers, obtain a disposable bootstrap session for the Makefile's authenticated raw-override preflight (do not print its token):\nTASK_MISTRAL_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=$(curl -fsS -c - -o /dev/null -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data '{\"username\":\"mistral_array_harness\",\"password\":\"harness-only-password\"}' http://localhost:3021/api/session/login | awk '$6==\"token\" {print $7}')\ntest -n \"$TASK_MISTRAL_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN\" && export BIFROST_E2E_AUTH_HEADER=\"Bearer $TASK_MISTRAL_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN\"\n6. Run the full owned setup/wire/cleanup chain in one Newman process:\nmake run-provider-harness-test PROVIDER=mistral FEATURE=\"mistral-content-array\" INCLUDE_PREVIEW=1 PARALLEL=0 COMPAT=off DB_VERIFY=0 SKIP_STREAM_CANCEL=1 ENV_FILE=tmp/mistral-content-array.env.json BASE_URL=http://localhost:3021\n7. The collection removes its provider/key, witness and login session. Invalidate the separate bootstrap session after the run, then stop the two foreground servers:\ncurl -fsS -X POST -H \"Authorization: $BIFROST_E2E_AUTH_HEADER\" http://localhost:3021/api/session/logout >/dev/null\nunset BIFROST_E2E_AUTH_HEADER TASK_MISTRAL_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN\nThe submitted rows are structurally validated; live execution belongs to the user. These eight calls reach only the local fixture, with a dummy key; no real provider credential is needed.",
